WEBVTT

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:15.850
Rikiishi...

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.710
I don't really understand it myself,

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:22.720
but I'm starting to feel like I can do something.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:44.370
Thank you. I'm sorry to have caused you all this trouble.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:46.810
I am so sorry.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.710
I'm going to need you to sign this.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:50.860
Yes, right away.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.740
Tange-san, you realize that you are his legal guardian?

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.700
You're gonna have to keep a close eye on him from now on.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.220
Hey, go on in.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.280
Joe!

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:14.360
You little... You really had us all worried! Where've you been?

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.030
Well...

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:18.300
I understand.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:20.410
You don't have to say a thing.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.150
I read it all in the papers.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:31.030
Guess your punches are as sharp as ever!

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.240
Let's go. Everyone's waiting for you.

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.930
Well, we'd better get going!

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.930
Watch him, now. If he gets into a fight again...

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:47.430
You won't be bailing him out!

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:51.260
Yes, I'm well aware of that. Thank you.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.060
Well, we'll be off.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:54.860
Let's go, Joe.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.150
One, two...

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:06.590
Joe!

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:07.580
Hey.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.240
Where've you been?

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.430
Yeah! You could've at least taken the time to write a postcard!

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:14.920
You had us all worried!

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.920
Sorry, sorry.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.090
We wouldn't need the police if "sorry" solved everything!

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.370
Bro Joe, ya really served your time well.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.930
That was perfect!

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.000
So, how have you all been?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.060
Right as rain on the plain!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.060
<i>We've been doing sumo!</i>

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.060
I won twelve straight matches the other day!

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.440
<i>But you turned tail when Taro challenged you.{edited down to avoid 3-liner}</i>

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.140
That's right, coward!

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:40.860
Now that's no fair.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:43.740
Excuse me, Yabuki-kun.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:50.670
U-Uh... We bought a van.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:52.140
Would you like to ride with us?

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:53.390
A van?

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.420
You got a new one?

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.880
Let's go for a ride, Bro Joe!

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.850
<i>We'll ride right through skid row!</i>

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.650
Come on, please?

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.380
<i>I guess Hayashi's getting good business now.</i>

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:06.130
It's all thanks to Nishi-kun. We've got more and more customers,

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:08.140
so my father splurged and bought it.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.640
But where's the driver?

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.900
You got your driver right here!

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.350
Nishi?

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:22.150
Yeah. Mr. Hayashi suggested that I get my license, and I just got it recently.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:29.620
Mammoth drives better than you'd think!

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.060
He gives us a ride from time to time.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.290
All right, guys!

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:37.290
Stop the chit-chat and get yourselves in!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.730
Yay! Let's go!

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.770
Go ahead and sit up front, Danpei-san.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:44.250
I'll get in the back with the children.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.550
It's fine. I'll get in the back.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:49.180
Come on.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.270
In you go!

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.180
All right, get in, you two!

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.540
And we're off!

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:14.230
Somebody's with somebody in the wheat fields...{an8 at qc suggestion}

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:17.960
What's wrong with them having a little kiss?

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:23.240
I don't have a special someone of my own, though...

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:28.110
Somebody's with somebody in the wheat fields...

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:32.680
Somebody's with somebody in the wheat fields...

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.350
Hey, keep it down back there!

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:36.730
I just got my license-you might get me into an accident!

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:40.230
They can't help it, Nishi-kun. They're all so happy.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.850
Why the hell did you just jump out like that?

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.140
Sorry...

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:08.220
So, where's Joe?

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.120
Joe's in the back!

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.220
Okay.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:13.920
Hey, guys! Joe's back!

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.350
Joe's back!

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:18.530
What the-?

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:19.790
You drunk again, wino?

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:21.360
Where's Joe!?

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.860
He's in the van!

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.170
Joe's come back!

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:26.360
That's good to hear!

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.330
Where are ya, Joe? Show yourself!

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:30.460
Come on everyone! It's Joe!

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:31.080
Show yourself!

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:32.120
Oh, there he is!

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.400
Hey, look! He's really back!

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.620
He's alive! See, he's moving!

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:42.130
Hey, where've you been all this time?

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:42.130
<i>I thought we were friends, Joe!</i>

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.190
I've been hearing rumors about you, Joe!

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:49.630
We were so lonely! Skid row is so boring without you!

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:53.390
Come on, let's see a little smile, Mr. President!

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:53.390
<i>What's the matter with ya?</i>

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:54.640
Cheer up, man!

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:58.440
My grandpa wouldn't stop asking when your next match was,

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.890
even when he was lying in bed, paralyzed!

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:06.400
Cheer up! We can't stand to see you looking down like that!

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:11.330
Well, Joe, you better get back on your feet so you can get back in the ring!

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.350
We're all here for you!

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:15.690
Yeah! We're here for you!

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:18.060
That's right!

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:18.680
<i>You better make it big as soon as you can!</i>

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.370
We're watching out for ya!

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:23.870
You're the hero of skid row! Got it?

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.510
Hear, hear!

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:27.330
Guys, that's enough!

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:31.640
Come on, out of our way!

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:33.390
I'm moving the van!

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.820
What, going already?

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:36.530
We barely even talked!

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.520
Mammoth, you cheapo!

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.400
Clear a path!

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.570
Joe! Stick it to 'em!

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:43.570
<i>Don't get too down!</i>

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:48.170
Rest up and make your big return-we'll be waiting for you!

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.170
<i>Go for it!</i>

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.880
We'll pool our money to buy you a great robe!

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:54.410
You're really something!

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.810
You're the champion of Namida Bridge!

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:59.430
The champion of Namida Bridge!

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:02.920
The champion of Namida Bridge!

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:06.740
The champion of Namida Bridge!

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.470
And we're here!

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:30.820
Yahoo!

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.150
First one out!

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:33.000
Heave-ho!

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.310
Go!

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:34.310
<i>What're you waiting for?</i>

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:34.750
Bro Joe!

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:35.320
Come on, get out!

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:37.920
Well, we made it!

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:38.330
Huh?

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:48.380
You must be tired after making that long trip in this cramped van.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.210
Thanks for the lift.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:17.840
Noriko-chan...

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:23.830
I'm so sorry, Noriko-chan. Joe's tired. Give him some slack.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.270
Oh, I wasn't...

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:33.710
Well, I'm going to make a meal to celebrate Yabuki-kun's return, so you children wait here!

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:35.460
Yeah! All right!

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:39.360
Listen. It's our job to act happy at times like these!

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.300
Can I make it?

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.810
Huh? Yes, please do.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:50.310
Well, I better get the van back to Hayashiya.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.190
Yeah, you do that.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:56.400
So...

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:59.320
Let's all go to the gym.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:00.760
Sure.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:31.050
Namida Bridge, huh?

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.850
You've made it all the way back here.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:35.480
But, Joe...

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:37.940
What are you gonna do now?

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.610
...in the wheat fields...

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:03.640
I don't have a...

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:10.140
Huh?

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.990
Cheer up, already!

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:23.030
Yabuki-kun's finally back, isn't he?

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:25.980
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:28.040
No matter what's happened, he's back.

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:29.880
Whatever his condition,

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:32.520
I gotta be grateful for that.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:33.510
Old man...

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:37.560
Take that!

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:46.130
And that's a wrap! That makes fifteen straight wins!

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:48.180
All right, I'm up next!

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:53.520
I'll put a stop to your winning streak!

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:56.140
Now, look each other in the eye... Get ready...

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:57.130
<i>Oh, wait! It's Mammoth!</i>

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:58.650
You're not fooling anyone!

00:11:58.650 --> 00:11:59.200
Gotcha!

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.570
But it's true! Yowch!

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.530
Oh, it really is Mammoth!

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.260
That's really Nishi, huh?

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.550
Hey, Bro, don't you think Mammoth's different?

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:30.860
Yeah. He sure has changed for the better.

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:33.020
I don't know what changed in his head,

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:36.100
but he suddenly transformed after you left!

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:42.900
Well, to put it simply, I think your disappearance

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:47.730
made Mammoth finally discover his passion, or something like that...

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:49.760
Through rain and shine,

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.650
he endured harsh weight loss and stuck it out through strict training.

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:56.580
I think that's pretty impressive.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:57.790
Yeah.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:04.760
Don't you have to go help out at Hayashiya?

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.840
Nah, I got a match coming up.

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.260
He gave me the day off.

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:10.760
A match?

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:15.700
Mammoth's having his first eight-round match at the end of next week!

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:16.770
Eight-round match?

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:24.530
I see. He's come a long way from the four-rounder I knew.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:30.330
Mammoth had two six-round matches while you were gone,

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.600
and he won them both by KO!

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:35.570
Yeah! We went to cheer him on!

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:36.790
By KO?

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:39.290
Joe...

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:45.760
You're really... really back!

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:07.480
You're...

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:11.780
looking one or two sizes bigger since I last saw you.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:16.620
It's all thanks to the time you hit me when I snuck out to eat udon.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:20.100
Well, I can't brag too much,

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:23.880
but I think I'm a bit better than I was back then.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:25.320
Just you watch!

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:26.020
Yeah.

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:28.010
All right, let's get to it!

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.000
How's that?

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:18.140
Come on in, everyone! Dinner's ready!

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:23.410
Let's go, Joe!

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:24.860
Yeah.

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.190
You guys freshened up around here.

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:09.730
Yeah. Everyone came in and cleaned the place up when we heard you were coming back.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.850
Go ahead, Yabuki-kun.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:15.490
Come to the table, Joe!

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.990
Joe, sit down right here.

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:29.590
No meat for you, Nishi-san. You've got a match coming up.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:33.490
Well, I could never go against you, Noriko...{no honorific for "han", as in ep 35}

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:35.940
A toast to Bro Joe!

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:34.370
<i>Fine, fine...{added}</i>

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:36.850
We'll have a toast with juice!

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.350
Cheers!

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:40.600
Yeah, cheers!

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.920
I gotta take a break.

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:09.220
Joe?

00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:15.040
Joe, what's gotten into you?

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:18.050
Noriko worked hard to make this meal for you!

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:19.880
I'll eat it later.

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.640
Joe! Eat her food!

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.690
H-Hold it, Joe!

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:31.570
Can't you at least say something nice to Noriko-chan first?

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:35.070
What are you talking about, Kinoko?

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:39.740
I-I mean, don't you want him to say something nice to you?

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:42.510
Besides, we've all done all this for him...

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:02.700
Joe's been through a lot. Let's leave him alone.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:36.480
Rikiishi...

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:42.990
I think I've gotten over my funk now that I'm finally back here.

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:48.660
If I hadn't...

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:02.630
If I hadn't come back, you wouldn't have been able to rest in peace.

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:35.000
A-Are you really still fiddling around with that?

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:38.630
How long do... do you need to be depressed until you're satisfied?

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:40.630
I'm done.

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:43.160
Wh-What?

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:51.600
I'm done being depressed.

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.100
I've finally decided to come back to the ring.

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:11.330
Old man!{added}

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:13.760
Ow, ow, ow...

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:16.750
That hurt!

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:19.810
That hurt!

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:23.470
Are you okay, old man?

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:24.300
Old man!

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:27.800
Joe... Joe said he's gonna stop being depressed!

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:32.560
He... He said he's gonna make a comeback!

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:34.810
Is that true, old man?

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:37.560
A comeback? You mean he's gonna box again?

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:38.990
Yeah, he sure is!

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:41.570
Joe's decided to come back to boxing!

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:43.820
Has he really?{added}

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:43.820
<i>Hooray!{added}</i>

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:47.060
Thank goodness for that!

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:52.670
Three cheers for Bro Joe!

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:52.670
<i>Hurrah!</i>

00:21:52.670 --> 00:21:54.720
Hurrah!

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:55.290
Way to go!

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:57.290
Way to go, Bro Joe!

00:21:56.350 --> 00:21:57.290
<i>Joe!</i>

00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:11.570
Joe... this isn't a dream, is it?{}{}{}{}

00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:15.770
I may be tired, but I ain't dreaming.

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:21.010
Nishi, look into my eyes.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:23.440
Are these the eyes of a dreamer?

00:22:28.090 --> 00:22:30.610
This guy named Gondo the Brawler told me

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:34.160
that Wolf's eyes are rotten, but mine are still alive.

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:41.520
No offense to Wolf, but I'm not Wolf.

00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:44.350
I'll never be like Wolf.

00:22:45.410 --> 00:22:46.460
I don't want to be like Wolf!

00:22:47.040 --> 00:23:07.150
I'm...

00:23:23.220 --> 00:23:25.500
I'm Yabuki Joe!

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:48.650
Yuke kouya wo

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:48.650
Go to the wilderness!

00:23:49.730 --> 00:23:52.480
Oira boxer

00:23:49.730 --> 00:23:52.480
I am a boxer.

00:23:53.280 --> 00:24:00.240
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:23:53.280 --> 00:24:00.240
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:05.910
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:05.910
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:07.960
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:07.960
Howling at the moon alone.

00:24:10.040 --> 00:24:14.170
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:24:10.040 --> 00:24:14.170
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:24:14.510 --> 00:24:17.510
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:24:14.510 --> 00:24:17.510
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

00:24:18.880 --> 00:24:21.800
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:18.880 --> 00:24:21.800
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:25.520
Oira boxer

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:25.520
I am a boxer.

00:24:26.640 --> 00:24:33.770
Asahi ga noboru yo otoko no mune ni {removed the Woo, but otherwise japanese is unchanged - Reed}

00:24:26.640 --> 00:24:33.770
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!

00:24:37.540 --> 00:24:38.980
Joe's eyes shine!

00:24:40.070 --> 00:24:42.000
His intense body blow...

00:24:42.000 --> 00:24:44.040
His killer punch bursts forth!

00:24:44.040 --> 00:24:46.170
Joe gets back in shape at a rapid pace!

00:24:47.230 --> 00:24:50.090
But his friend Nishi

00:24:50.090 --> 00:24:53.570
finds a definite weakness in Joe, who can only attack the body.

00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:57.850
Before long, Joe is greatly injured.

00:24:58.640 --> 00:25:03.930
Now, as Joe's fighting spirit burns, spurring my and Nishi's unease,

00:25:03.930 --> 00:25:05.600
which way is tomorrow!?
